<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Korean, a draft not yet read by a fluent reviewer (#495). The notes on each string are in values/strings.xml.
    Polite 해요체 in sentences (-요, -하세요), short nouns on buttons and labels (로그인, 다시 시도, 취소, 다음).
    "Vehicle" is 차량, never the word for bus; "run" is 배차 (a timetabled departure, "오전 6:43 배차");
    "trip" is 운행 (운행 시작, 운행 종료, 운행 재개); "report" is 위치 전송, counted with 건 ("142건 전송");
    "dispatcher" is 관제실; "block" is 블록; "agency" is 회사; "route" is 노선; "stop" is 정류장;
    "rider" is 승객; "driver" is 기사; "phone" is 휴대전화, as Android's own screens say; the route sign is 행선판.
    A placeholder is never followed by a particle that changes with the word before it (을/를, 이/가, 은/는):
    only 에, 에서, 의, or a noun such as 차량 %1$s, 노선 %1$s, %1$s 방면, %1$s 배차.
-->
